  "description": "Your Bokeh Ti Frameset\n\nTHE LATEST EVOLUTION OF OUR UNIQUE MASON BOKEH Ti FRAMESET\n\nA world-leading, finely finished, titanium multi-condition frameset, welded and finished by a long-established, highly experienced maker in Tuscany, Italy. Our latest version of this very special special bicycle brings a host of improvements and updates.\n\nWorking with Dedacciai, we have developed a new titanium tubeset. New seatstays boost tyre clearance and comfort to unparalleled levels. New chainstays are carefully profiled to match this enhanced tyre clearance, while forming a stable partnership with an enlarged T47 bottom bracket. New MASON-designed titanium dropouts are 3D-printed, with Universal Derailleur Hanger compatibility. The BokehTi is welded in small batches and is available on a pre-order basis only.\n\nThe new BokehTi frameset is completed by the Rangefinder fork – a MASON-designed carbon fork optimised for the same versatile tyre clearance.\n\nImproved internal routing brings cables and hoses through the bottom bracket and chainstays. Rear derailleur cables, mechanical or electronic, emerge from the 3D-printed structure of the Bokeh Ti's new dropouts. Dedicated dynamo routing through the top tube now combines year-round practicality with stylish design.\n\nWith Tuscany-made craftsmanship and super-high finish quality, the BokehTi is your versatile friend for fast adventure and fun-filled bikepacking trips. Highly customisable build levels make the limited production Mason BokehTi a very special companion indeed.\n\nMASON CUSTOM PROGRAMME\n\nWe love building individual bicycles for individual people. All MASON models are open to and carefully designed build levels.\n\nWhile your frame is being welded and carefully finished you also have the chance to specify a full ‘Mason Custom Build’, basing your finished bicycle on a choice of components from our various carefully chosen suppliers. Please contact us for further information on this process and to start your dream build.\n\nDedacciai titanium frame, with revised seatstays and chainstays\n\nGenerously eyeletted for maximum expedition flexibility\n\nMASON Rangefinder carbon fork with multiple equipment eyelets and dynamo routing\n\nFull set of high-grade, stainless steel accessory mounting screws and small parts, including cable routing parts and MASON Multiport inserts, supplied with frameset.\n\nMASON Penta carbon microadjust seatpost and MASON Macro seatclamp included (MASON Sensor titanium post available as upgrade)",
